(function () {
  var m = {"AIM101-S": {"abstract": "Distributed edge assets, remote sensors, and transactional systems often leave operational data isolated from cloud AI platforms. This session demonstrates how to break down these boundaries using Cloudera Anywhere Cloud. Discover an event-driven architectural blueprint that standardizes real-time streaming on-premises, unifies hybrid pipelines, and lands telemetry directly into Cloudera’s Open Data Lakehouse on AWS. Learn how grounding autonomous AI agents on AWS with continuous edge context simplifies data sovereignty, eliminates bottlenecks, and enables real-time, closed-loop enterprise automation. This presentation is brought to you by Cloudera, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM102-S": {"abstract": "AI-generated code is scaling fast, but its security performance is not keeping up. Across more than 100 models tested since 2023, the average security pass rate remains stuck at 56%, even as syntax performance approaches perfection. For security leaders, this is no longer a developer tooling discussion. It is a verification, release-control, and accountability issue. In this session, Veracode leaders unpack the findings from the 2026 GenAI Code Security Report and turn them into practical actions for secure software delivery at scale. Whether you’re a developer, security lead, or business decision-maker, this session will help you navigate the real-world security implications of GenAI in your development workflow. This presentation is brought to you by Veracode, Inc., an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM103-S": {"abstract": "Making a big impact always starts small - a dream, an idea, a hope. Brian Martin - co-founder of Rare Hopes NFP and CTO of Applied AI at Cloudera - will share the story of the non-profit he and industry colleagues founded with the support of AWS, Cloudera, and other companies to deliver a multi-million dollar equivalent platform supporting drug repurposing for rare disease hypothesis generation. Illustrating the concept and components necessary to deliver this advanced graph analytical approach to transforming knowledge into insights, the story demonstrates the power and potential that AI brings allowing companies to work with knowledge - not just data. This presentation is brought to you by Cloudera, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM104-S": {"abstract": "Incident investigation still consumes 1-2 hours of engineering time per event. See how New Relic's Intelligent Observability Platform integrates with AWS DevOps Agent to: Autonomously triage incidents, pinpoint root cause, and deliver actionable remediation with no custom tooling required. Investigate incidents agentically correlating telemetry, code, and deployments across AWS, multi cloud, and on-prem environments. Demonstrate how this innovation proactively prevents future incidents by analyzing patterns and recommending improvements. Learn how customers are cutting MTTR by 75% and shifting from firefighting to prevention, and walk away ready to get started. This presentation is brought to you by New Relic, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM105-S": {"abstract": "Barclays is transforming finance operations through an AWS-powered AI platform that combines Generative AI, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), vector knowledge bases, and Agentic AI. The platform unifies structured and unstructured finance data to automate SOX controls, enhance management reporting, enable finance data enrichment, and support intelligent decision-making across strategic finance initiatives. Built with enterprise-grade governance, explainability, and auditability, the solution helps strengthen control effectiveness, improve regulatory compliance, and accelerate reporting outcomes. Learn how AI-powered agents, explainable workflows, and governed human-in-the-loop processes are driving operational efficiency, enhancing regulatory confidence, improving audit readiness, and laying the foundation for autonomous finance operations. This presentation is brought to you by Capgemini, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM106-S": {"abstract": "Human review can't scale linearly with generative-AI volume. Vanguard's AI Center of Excellence built a closed-loop oversight system where every AI response is scored by an LLM-as-judge, confirmed or overturned by a subject-matter expert, and routed through a confusion matrix: confirmed catches sharpen the agent, disagreements calibrate the judge. Each SME label grows a benchmark that resets how much oversight the next cycle needs, proving mathematically that coverage can fall while risk holds flat. Built on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, Lambda-hosted detector SLMs, SQS, DynamoDB, and SageMaker, the loop moves toward real-time interruption of harmful responses before customers see them. This presentation is brought to you by Capgemini, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM107-S": {"abstract": "AI is shipping more code to production than ever before, but incidents are taking longer to resolve. Hear from peers at different stages of operational maturity, all testing out ways to put AI and automation to work so their teams get more time back for innovation. Panelists will share how they decide what's safe to automate outright, where to keep a human in or on the loop, and where full human judgment still matters. You'll hear what convinced them to hand over more control, what happened when it didn't go as planned, and how they cut toil without losing their grip on the systems they're accountable for. This presentation is brought to you by PagerDuty, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM108-S": {"abstract": "Mortgage lending still runs on handoffs, exceptions, and manual review. See how a leading US mortgage lender is rebuilding origination and servicing with agentic AI on AWS, cutting cycle times while keeping controls and auditability intact. We will also show how the same agent patterns reach IT operations, resolving incidents before customers feel them. Tata Consultancy Services shares the reference architecture, guardrails, and adoption model behind both. Built for financial services business and operations leaders, CIOs and IT operations heads, and data and AI leaders, this session gives you a practical path from promising pilots to production at enterprise scale. This presentation is brought to you by Tata Consultancy Services, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM109-S": {"abstract": "AI agents behave (and fail) in unpredictable and nuanced ways that erode customer trust before engineering teams know anything is wrong. Teams want to deploy agents into critical business workflows, but it's hard to know if agents are behaving as intended or returning wrong answers.​ ​ In this talk, you’ll learn how to observe the entire AI stack, optimize tokenomics, and see a demo on how to evaluate and control agent behavior with guardrails to stop harmful or inaccurate outputs. All of this can be done in near real- time and at low cost.​ This presentation is brought to you by Splunk, a Cisco Company, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM110-S": {"abstract": "The UK Home Office is tasked with keeping the UK Safe and Prosperous. Capgemini is working with the Home Office to increase effectiveness and efficiency of its digital and cloud services. Key areas include case management, legacy modernization and SDLC efficiency. This is being delivered in collaboration with AWS and Anthropic. Using Claude agents via AWS Bedrock, this capability is forecast to deliver >30% cashable savings compared to existing processes and improve quality by >20% through better informed decisions. This presentation is brought to you by Capgemini, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM111-S": {"abstract": "Successful enterprise AI depends on more than just the latest models. It requires context that connects knowledge across systems, intelligence that turns information into useful action, and protection that preserves permissions, security, and trust. This session presents a practical foundation for deploying AI across the enterprise—using AWS and Bedrock to move from isolated pilots to governed workflows. Learn how leaders are designing for adoption, measurable outcomes, and continuous improvement from the start. This presentation is brought to you by Glean, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM112-S": {"abstract": "Enterprises connecting AI agents to systems of record face three unsolved problems: can an agent discover what data exists and what it means, get that context without runaway token cost, and touch only what it's authorized to touch. GraphQL, the proven Linux Foundation-backed standard beneath many of the world's largest customer experiences at brands like Netflix, AirBnB, Shopify, Walmart, and countless others, already solves all three through self-describing schemas and field-level queries. This talk lays out the architecture for combining GraphQL with MCP, including Apollo's approach to graph-based orchestration for cost and reliability. This presentation is brought to you by Apollo GraphQL, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM113-S": {"abstract": "Cloud data infrastructure rarely stays optimal — workloads change, configurations drift, and data infrastructure expertise is scarce. AIOps applies AI-powered, agentic automation to cloud data storage operations: continuously assessing the environment, analyzing it against workload-specific best practices, recommending fixes, and applying them at the level of autonomy you choose. In this lightning talk, we’ll explore how NetApp Workload Factory does all this while providing customers with right-sized cost, on-target performance, stronger resilience and protection — without the need for deep data infrastructure expertise, and while always staying in control. This presentation is brought to you by NetApp, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM115-S": {"abstract": "Enterprises are moving from a handful of agents to hundreds. Without a shared layer for identity, policy, orchestration, and observability, that growth stalls. In this 20-minute launch session, we introduce the Agentic AI Control Plane on AWS: a governed foundation for building, deploying, and running agents across business and IT workflows. See how it handles agent onboarding, guardrails, cost and performance visibility, and human oversight, with a live look at the platform. Built for CIOs, data and AI leaders, and platform and risk teams who need agent fleets to scale safely, with the controls their auditors expect. This presentation is brought to you by Tata Consultancy Services, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM116-S": {"abstract": "To unlock transformative business outcomes, AI agents require a foundation of trusted data with rich enterprise context. Delivering success means bridging the knowledge, trust, and action gaps across a highly complex data landscape. In this session, learn how Informatica Intelligent Data Management Cloud (IDMC) provides the comprehensive AI-ready data needed to power reliable agentic workflows. Explore how headless IDMC architecture via integrations with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, Agent Registry and Amazon Quick fuels agents with trusted enterprise context and end-to-end governance, driving impactful results and long-term project success.", "language": "en"},"AIM118-S": {"abstract": "Frontier voice agents are already handling live customer calls inside health systems, banks and insurers, without audio ever leaving the customer's AWS account. This session covers the architecture that makes that possible, from in-VPC deployment and zero data retention to integration with their existing stack. Working from a production deployment taking real calls, we walk through the latency budget that keeps conversational voice feeling human, the trade-offs private deployment brings, and how to size it for your own environment. Leave with an understanding of where ElevenAgents fits in your current environment, a reference architecture and a deployment checklist. This presentation is brought to you by ElevenLabs, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM119-S": {"abstract": "Disconnected systems slow teams down. See how Agentforce, Slack and AgentCore Bedrock enable your Headless agentic strategy to unlock seamless collaboration and boost productivity across teams in real time. This presentation is brought to you by Salesforce, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM120-S": {"abstract": "Modern service demands always-on, personalized experiences. See how Agentforce Service and Slack partner with Amazon Connect Customer, so you can cut handle times, costs & boost CSAT. This presentation is brought to you by Salesforce, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM121-S": {"abstract": "Ontology has become one of the defining ideas in enterprise AI. Every cloud and data platform now claims to have one. They rarely converge on the same structure, conventions, or architecture. Those differences determine whether an ontology can support agentic AI. That test comes down to three things: how it's structured, how it's generated from the systems and context already in place, and how it stays current as the business changes. This talk lays out the practical requirements for an ontology built for agentic AI, drawing on the architecture TextQL runs across the messiest data estates at Fortune 50 companies. This presentation is brought to you by TextQL, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM122-S": {"abstract": "Financial services depend on software that needs to be available around the clock. When that software fails, the consequences can affect millions of customers and create regulatory, financial, and reputational risk. This panel brings together technology leaders from some of the world’s largest financial institutions across banking, payments, and investment management for a conversation moderated by Anish Agrawal, CEO & Cofounder of Traversal, the AI SRE helping diagnose, fix, and prevent incidents across complex enterprise environments. Together, they’ll discuss how AI is changing production reliability across financial services, where it’s already being used, the emerging role of AI SREs, what teams look for when evaluating new approaches, and what it takes to deploy AI safely in highly regulated environments. This presentation is brought to you by Traversal, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM123-S": {"abstract": "AI is rapidly becoming one of the biggest drivers of productivity and innovation in the enterprise — and one of the fastest-growing sources of data security risk. As copilots, assistants, and public AI tools become integrated into daily work, sensitive data is flowing into systems that most security teams can’t fully see, understand, or control. The problem is that traditional data security controls were never built for this. In fact, many organizations were already struggling to operationalize data security before AI accelerated the challenge. The good news? AI isn’t just creating the problem — it’s also enabling a smarter, more effective way to solve it. Attendees will leave with a clearer understanding of how AI is reshaping data security — and how they can use that same technology to gain control, minimize exposure, and support safer AI adoption across the business. This presentation is brought to you by Concentric AI, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM124-S": {"abstract": "AI without workflows is just expensive advice. The next generation of AI leaders are moving beyond disconnected copilots and isolated use cases to reinvent how work gets done. Join ServiceNow to learn how the AI Control Tower for Business Reinvention helps organizations govern AI, connect enterprise data, and orchestrate work across every agent, model, and workflow. Discover how AI that thinks and workflows that act enable enterprises to deploy AI quickly while maintaining trust, security, and control. This presentation is brought to you by ServiceNow, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM125-S": {"abstract": "Deploying agents at scale is a major endeavor for any organization; in healthcare, the stakes are especially high. Unpredictable behaviors & unreliable outputs pose a risk to patients, invite scrutiny from regulators, & erode hard-won institutional trust. Regulated industries must balance accuracy alongside their drive to innovate. Barr Moses, co-founder & CEO of Monte Carlo, will delve into this challenging topic with leaders from GE Healthcare. They’ll dissect some of the most difficult failure modes for agents & discuss how reliability practices have to evolve as teams scale agentic workflows in high-stakes environments. Discussed: how AI itself can be turned back on the problem of observing, resolving, and optimizing agents as well as building the guardrails, ownership models, & trust infrastructure that let a highly regulated organization move quickly without compromising on trust. This presentation is brought to you by Monte Carlo, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM126-S": {"abstract": "Iberdrola, a Spanish multinational electric utility company, is transforming marketing with CreatIA, an agentic AI platform co-developed with Accenture and AWS. Facing rising demand for content, faster decisions and accelerated campaign delivery, Iberdrola adopted a new operating model powered by specialized AI agents across the marketing lifecycle. CreatIA unifies market intelligence, insights generation, content creation, validation and campaign activation in a single enterprise platform. The solution has reduced time spent analyzing and processing information by 80%, accelerated strategic decision making by 40%, increased creative production capacity by up to four times, and reduced content production costs by 60%. This presentation is brought to you by Accenture, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM129-S": {"abstract": "How does a nationally owned bank out-innovate much larger competitors? Kiwibank, New Zealand's only 100% NZ-owned bank, must compete against four far larger Australian-owned banks — with a fraction of the resources. Working with Accenture and AWS, Kiwibank is building a governed enterprise AI layer that every future application can draw from. The result: a compounding AI advantage that grows with each new use case, letting the bank launch products faster, serve customers more intelligently, and scale without proportional cost growth. Hear how Kiwibank is using Accenture and AWS to build the AI foundation for its next decade of growth. This presentation is brought to you by Accenture, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM130-S": {"abstract": "Cox Communications partnered with Accenture and Anthropic's Claude on AWS to transform B2B marketing and sales, generating a 7x return on its first-year AI investment. By deploying AI-powered marketing and sales agents across 120 micro-industries and eight customer segments, Cox replaced one-size-fits-all campaigns with personalized engagement at scale. The initiative delivered 55% faster speed to market, a 2-point increase in B2B conversion, 40% higher campaign efficiency, and an 86% reduction in lead management costs while improving data accuracy from 18% to 97%. Today, Cox is operating an end-to-end agentic go-to-market system with human oversight. This presentation is brought to you by Accenture, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM131-S": {"abstract": "SoCalGas is migrating its decades-old Customer Information System to SAP IS-U, where hypercare is the highest-risk phase for customer and regulatory impacts. Traditional command centers require teams to manually correlate signals across ServiceNow, Azure DevOps, dashboards, logs, and staffing systems, slowing response times. To improve visibility and decision making, Accenture built a multi-agent AI command center on Amazon Bedrock. A Commander agent orchestrates Platform Health, Business KPI, Knowledge, and Situational Awareness agents, while every recommendation is citation-grounded and human-supervised. Learn how agentic AI is helping SoCalGas unify operational intelligence in a mission-critical utility environment. This presentation is brought to you by Accenture, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM132-S": {"abstract": "Govern enterprise AI: Optimize costs, control prompt risks, and gain visibility with Cribl and AWS. This presentation is brought to you by Cribl, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM133-S": {"abstract": "Agentic AI is making ERP modernization more urgent than ever. To coordinate decisions across the organization enterprise, AI must be grounded in a modern cloud ERP foundation—one that connects data, processes, business rules, and controls. ERP is no longer just where work is recorded. It has become the operational foundation that enables enterprise agentic AI and ultimately the Autonomous Enterprise.​ SAP and AWS are partnering to help clients accelerate their AI vision Autonomous Enterprise where people set direction, AI executes operational tasks, and organizations respond faster to change leveraging a single intelligent system with full business context. Join us to explore how SAP on AWS helps moves organizations of all sizes to move beyond isolated AI pilots to enterprise-wide outcomes delivered with reliability and confidence.​ This presentation is brought to you by SAP, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM134-S": {"abstract": "Software is becoming more than something companies build. It is becoming the system through which they improve. The next generation of software factories will turn business signals into production software, measure the outcomes, and use those outcomes to improve each cycle of development. Engineers set the goals, architecture, policies, and approval gates, while the system handles execution and continuously improves itself. Factory cofounder Eno Reyes will share what this future looks like, what has to be true to build it, and why self-improving software will fundamentally change how every company operates. This presentation is brought to you by Factory, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM135-S": {"abstract": "Most organizations are currently stuck between two worlds: the urgent need to adopt AI to remain competitive, & the critical mandate to protect corporate data & reputation. AI is evolving faster than any tool in IT history, and faster than any organization can keep up with. The temptation to simply block access to AI is strong, but just saying \"No\" means ceding the advantage to those able to say \"Yes!\". The 3 Pillars of a \"Secure Yes\": Visibility: Knowing what AI is being used across the org. Accountability: Defining who owns the data & the output. Resilience: Building frameworks that adapt as regulations change. In this session, we will outline the framework for secure AI adoption. We will move past the hype to discuss how leaders can build visibility, maintain accountability, and foster a culture of responsible innovation. This presentation is brought to you by Island, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM137-S": {"abstract": "Customers expect fast, personalized, and seamless experiences across every interaction with a brand. For Tapestry, connecting consumer feedback, sentiment, and operational signals is key to identifying issues that can impact customer experience and brand reputation. In this session, Sonal Sharan will share how Tapestry is leveraging ignio's AI Agents to continuously analyze these signals, surface emerging concerns, and provide real-time visibility into business-impacting issues. Intelligent workflows help prioritize and route issues for faster resolution, while actionable insights support more proactive customer engagement, resulting in a more connected, responsive, and customer-centric organization delivering exceptional experiences across Tapestry’s leading brands. This presentation is brought to you by Digitate, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM138-S": {"abstract": "AI is entering a new era: from static generation to live experiences. From shopping to entertainment, digital experiences are becoming live, visual, and personalized. In this session, Decart will explore the infrastructure powering this shift, what it takes to deliver AI-generated video in real time, and how to bring these experiences to scale. Join us for a look at the technology behind Live AI, and where it’s going next. This presentation is brought to you by Decart, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM201": {"abstract": "If you've ever wanted to know more about the environmental impact of your cloud usage, this session is for you. In this lightning talk, learn about the latest features of the AWS Sustainability service, including expanded impact areas beyond carbon, increased data granularity, and programmatic access via APIs. We walk through how to use the service to track progress against your sustainability goals and integrate environmental data into your existing workflows and reporting processes. Whether you're just getting started or already reporting on cloud emissions, this session has you covered.", "language": "en"},"AIM204": {"abstract": "The AI experiment is over. Now it has to work. This session walks through the AWS AI Platform end-to-end, starting at the chip layer with AWS Trainium and AWS Graviton delivering up to 40% better price performance. From there, model inference and customization through Amazon Bedrock and Amazon SageMaker AI. Then production agents on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore. Every layer co-designed so workloads move across the stack without rearchitecting. You will leave knowing which service handles which job, where the layers connect to accelerate production timelines, and how to keep your architecture open as your AI strategy evolves.", "language": "en"},"AIM205": {"abstract": "AI is accelerating sustainability at unprecedented speed, but only if the infrastructure behind it keeps pace. In this session, we will explore how AWS makes AI infrastructure more sustainable through hardware design decisions that minimize embodied carbon, custom silicon optimized for energy efficiency, and ML-driven data center optimization. Amazon Operations will show how AI and ML turn facility maintenance into prescriptive, autonomous operations: optimizing HVAC, water, and utilities for greater equipment reliability, and sustainability. Leave with a clear understanding of the AWS services powering these solutions, how AWS is building a more sustainable infrastructure, and how to get started with tracking and reducing your environmental impact.", "language": "en"},"AIM206": {"abstract": "Data sovereignty, data gravity, and latency requirements prevent many organizations from running all AI workloads in the public cloud. AWS AI Factories bring AWS and NVIDIA AI infrastructure directly into your data center, fully operated, maintained, and continuously updated by AWS. Run leading foundation models on premises for training and inference without building and managing AI infrastructure yourself or negotiating separate agreements with model providers. In this session, learn how organizations are accelerating AI adoption, reducing time to value, and maintaining full control of their data while benefiting from the AWS experience in their own facilities.", "language": "en"},"AIM211": {"abstract": "Every AI breakthrough demands innovation across the full stack: chips, servers, software, and the models built on top, each layer making the next one faster and cheaper to run. In this session, discover how AWS and frontier AI builders drive full-stack innovation on AWS Trainium to scale post-training and reinforcement learning, serve at high throughput, and bend the cost-per-token curve. Examine real architectural decisions from silicon to application, then look ahead to what's next in Trainium and AWS infrastructure. You will see how each layer of innovation compounds and learn where to place your bets on AI infrastructure.", "language": "en"},"AIM212": {"abstract": "Ship agents fast. Connect to anything. Optimize continuously. In this session, learn best practices for the full agent lifecycle on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore. Build: go from local to production with microVM isolation, persistent memory, and any framework. Connect: access MCP servers, knowledge bases, and APIs through Gateway with automatic authentication. Optimize: trace every model call with OpenTelemetry-compatible observability and run continuous evaluations. Walk away with architectural patterns and implementation strategies to ship your first agent in minutes, not months.", "language": "en"},"AIM213": {"abstract": "When adversaries move in seconds, security has to move faster. CrowdStrike shares how they built scalable, real-time LLM inference on Amazon SageMaker to power threat detection at massive scale, where sub-second latency is a hard requirement. Learn how dedicated, configurable endpoints gave them full control over performance, while SageMaker AI's managed infrastructure removed the operational overhead. Walk away with a blueprint for running latency-critical workloads on SageMaker Managed Inference, without running the stack yourself.", "language": "en"},"AIM214": {"abstract": "Enterprises that own their AI lifecycle across training and inference can adapt their models as fast as their users' need change. Vanguard outgrew off the shelf models and built infrastructure that runs custom large language models (LLMs) and specialized small language models (SLMs) side by side. Go inside the implementation to see how Amazon SageMaker HyperPod powers resilient multi node training and high throughput inference. Hear lessons from engineering alongside AWS product teams.", "language": "en"},"AIM216": {"abstract": "Accelerate intelligent document processing with Amazon Textract Abstract - Building custom extraction pipelines on foundation models is powerful but expensive to maintain. Textract Intelligence gives you the same GenAI flexibility as a managed service: custom-field extraction, document classification, splitting, and summarization, all backed by purpose-built OCR instead of a vision model guessing at pixels. In this session we compare approaches head-to-head on accuracy, latency, and cost, then show how 40-language support and trustworthy confidence scores close the gaps that push teams to DIY solutions.", "language": "en"},"AIM217": {"abstract": "Give your applications a voice and ears. This session shows how Amazon Transcribe converts speech to text and Amazon Polly turns text into lifelike speech. See how to build real-time voice agents, and multilingual experiences, with practical patterns for latency, accuracy, and scale.", "language": "en"},"AIM218": {"abstract": "We'll explore how bidirectional audio streaming enables natural, low-latency dialogue, with expressive voices across multiple languages. See how new capabilities like cross-modal voice-and-text switching, asynchronous tool calling for multi-step tasks, and a large context window let you build voice agents, customer service automation, and conversational apps.", "language": "en"},"AIM219": {"abstract": "Managing software procurement across dozens of tools, teams, and accounts is slow and error-prone. In this lightning talk, we use AI agents to automate the buyer journey on AWS Marketplace to discover and evaluate products, accept discounted offers instantly, enforce governance, achieve operational excellence, request refunds and cancellations, and gain unified visibility into spend and cost management. Compress procurement from weeks to minutes while maintaining governance and financial controls.", "language": "en"},"AIM220": {"abstract": "AI moves fast: new models, new economics, and new governance capabilities. Attend this breakout to learn about the latest innovations across Amazon Bedrock. We cover recent model additions from OpenAI, Anthropic, and more, along with advances in inference and updates across security, governance, and cost management. Whether you are new to Bedrock or want to keep up with the latest releases, this session offers something for everyone. Leave knowing what is available today and where to focus next.", "language": "en"},"AIM2200-S": {"abstract": "TeleTracking's platform is air traffic control for hospitals: 200K+ beds and 100+ command centers depend on it. Re-platforming onto an AI-native foundation has taken its service-to-engineer ratio from 6:1 to 30:1. The lever isn't headcount: It’s relying on one agent to pair gcx and the Grafana Cloud MCP server with AWS MCP tooling. Oren Lion replays an MSK incident where Grafana Assistant identified a cluster-wide broker disruption in minutes, pairing Frontend Observability with Amazon CloudFront to line up what hurt with what changed. He closes with Assistant Investigations, read-only guardrails, and a recipe you can run yourself.. This presentation is brought to you by Grafana Labs, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2201-S": {"abstract": "Every major technology shift starts the same way. We use new technology to do the old thing. Early factories replaced steam engines with electric motors, but real transformation came when they redesigned the factory around what electricity made possible. We’re doing the same thing with AI. AI transformation isn’t about adding agents to existing workflows. It’s about redesigning how work gets done. That starts with context. In this session, we’ll show how teams can make work visible, give humans and AI a shared understanding of it, redesign workflows around agents, and turn that understanding into action. This presentation is brought to you by Lucid Software, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2202-S": {"abstract": "Enterprise AI requires scalable, multi-agentic workflows capable of handling complex reasoning without sacrificing real-time speed. This session explores how Capital One designs proprietary multi-agent systems on AWS, optimized for governance, performance, and reliability. You’ll hear how state-of-the-art serving frameworks like vLLM, efficient distributed serving platforms like llm-d, and advanced agentic inference optimization techniques can enhance latency and boost throughput. We’ll showcase these principles through real-world applications, including complex real employee- and customer-facing banking use cases while meeting rigorous business standards around accuracy, reliability, and risk management. This presentation is brought to you by Capital One, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2203-S": {"abstract": "AI agents are actively running code, accessing databases, and making critical business decisions across every industry. But as these systems gain independence, they also introduce complex security risks throughout their lifecycle. Are you ready to protect a system that learns and acts on its own as your organization embarks on the AI journey? Join our panel of top AI and cybersecurity experts as they break down the end-to-end security of AI systems and agentic applications. We will explore real-world customer challenges and share practical strategies to safeguard autonomous agents across cloud and on-premises environments. This presentation is brought to you by Fortinet, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2204-S": {"abstract": "Verify, don't trust: a reproducible needle test that surfaces undeclared upstream calls in any stack. This presentation is brought to you by Brave, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2205": {"abstract": "Forge accelerates AI solution development on AWS. In this session, learn about Forge's capabilities and how to use them to create custom evaluations for your use case, incorporate your data into your AI solution, and select the right model for your needs.", "language": "en"},"AIM2206-S": {"abstract": "As enterprises move from experimenting with AI agents to deploying them at scale, the challenge is no longer just how to build agents, it’s how to maintain visibility, performance, and control across the growing agent ecosystem. This session will explore how Amazon Bedrock and Dataiku Agent Management support the agent lifecycle from creation through enterprise-wide management. Attendees will see how organizations can build and deploy agents with AWS while using Dataiku to discover agents, monitor performance, and identify risk across environments, helping teams scale agentic AI with greater confidence and governance. This presentation is brought to you by Dataiku, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2207-S": {"abstract": "Yeah, yeah, AI SOC, we get it. But what really goes into getting wins out of AI in security vs saving a couple of clicks? This talk will show the importance of small (dumb) LLM's and how they create opportunities for secops by allowing you to use more tokens, anywhere you want. It will demo how you can go beyond enriching a few alerts to stack rank your most valuable security tools in an ROI thunderdome. You'll learn the AI confidence guardrail framework you need so you to actually start taking actions on your behalf without accidentally deleting all your VM's when you asked it to \"eliminate all vulnerabilities.\" Seeing is believing, so there will be real-world demos of where AI works, where it doesn't, and why--bring your 3D glasses. This presentation is brought to you by Trellix, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2208-S": {"abstract": "The AI revolution is upending organizations’ security and GRC programs. Shadow AI is exploding as employees adopt new agent harnesses, workflows, platforms, and plugins. Even sanctioned AI poses new challenges that don’t yet have standardized solutions. Meanwhile, developers are moving AI applications from experimentation to production, introducing new risks. This session will break down what AI Governance is all about, cover common concerns that it’s meant to resolve, and provide attendees with practical tips for solving some of their most pressing AI Governance challenges. What you’ll learn. What AI Governance entails, from practical policy to active protections. How to solve AI Governance concerns across different layers of the AI stack. This presentation is brought to you by Vanta, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2209-S": {"abstract": "Philips faced a 45-day sales quoting bottleneck in digital pathology, chasing systems and spreadsheets on every deal. With EPAM and AWS, Philips built Sensei, a conversational AI sales agent, using an AI-native SDLC powered by AWS Kiro and running on Amazon Bedrock with Strands Agents. In under six months, specialized agents for pricing, quoting and CRM cut quote turnaround by 90 percent, generating customer briefings in under two minutes, with governance and compliance built in for a regulated industry. This session shares a practical blueprint for applying agentic AI to complex enterprise workflows at speed, without sacrificing enterprise-grade trust. This presentation is brought to you by EPAM, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM221-S": {"abstract": "Companies have shifted from talking about agents to putting them to work, but moving from an AWS Bedrock AgentCore demo to a governed, production multi-agent system inside a regulated enterprise isn't a straight line. Atos will show what that path looks like, where it breaks, and how to fix it. What you'll learn ⮚Enterprise patterns that separate successful AWS agentic AI deployments from stalled pilots ⮚Building a governance layer on Amazon Bedrock that regulated industries will approve ⮚How GSI partners turn ideas into completed, production-ready deployments ⮚Where AWS tooling is mature, where it's still evolving, and how to architect around the gaps This presentation is brought to you by Atos, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2210": {"abstract": "A large-scale AI workload can run for weeks across thousands of interconnected GPUs, where a single failure or security gap can be costly. Amazon EC2 brings together a portfolio of accelerated computing instances and innovations that keep the most demanding AI workloads secure by default and resilient to failures and maintenance. In this session, discover what's new in the AWS accelerated compute portfolio and dive deep into the architecture behind the latest generation of GPU instances for training and inference across large language and multimodal models. Hear real-world examples of how leading companies build on AWS, and leave understanding how AWS accelerated computing enables AI at scale.", "language": "en"},"AIM2212-S": {"abstract": "The hype machine says AI makes developers faster. This was true in 2025, when 68% of devs said they were saving 10 hours per week, but we’re not in 2025. Our 2026 data shows only 26% of devs are still saving 10 hours per week, but are facing more bottlenecks with increasing levels of cognitive load. The role of a developer has shifted, with organisations moving from AI adoption to looking for impact. This is presenting developers with new opportunities and challenges. What are the organisations and developers who are moving faster, and delivering at a higher quality point doing differently to those still looking for impact? In this session, we’ll explore the results from the latest State of DevEx report, diving into how developer roles have changed, and how you can unlock the transformational power of AI. This presentation is brought to you by Atlassian, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM2213": {"abstract": "Hear from four AI leaders building experiences that didn't exist a year ago: real-time video generation, world models, physical AI, and LLMs for drug discovery. These breakthroughs demand both high performance and low cost to work at all. AWS Trainium helped turn that future into production reality. Each panelist walks through their use case: the specific technical barrier they hit, how they used Trainium to get past it, and what shipping it to customers unlocked.", "language": "en"},"AIM222-S": {"abstract": "Join this exclusive hands-on workshop to master building and deploying high-impact AI agents with Cloudera Agent Studio. Move from experimentation to production using trusted data, scalable workflows, and governed infrastructure. Led by Cloudera solution architects, you will build multi-agent workflows without code, develop agentic chatbots for data access, learn Model Context Protocol (MCP) integration with AWS tools including Amazon Bedrock and PuppyGraph, and explore the latest Cloudera AI and Workbench enhancements. Designed for data scientists, developers, engineers, and analysts ready to enable secure, scalable, open AI across hybrid environments. This presentation is brought to you by Cloudera, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM223-S": {"abstract": "AI is accelerating innovation — and accelerating attackers. From prompt injection and data exfiltration to cloud privilege escalation, adversaries are increasingly exploiting AI-powered architectures to move faster than traditional defenses. In this session, AWS and CrowdStrike experts will demonstrate how organizations can securely build and defend modern AI workloads running on AWS. Attendees will explore real-world architectures using Amazon Bedrock and AgentCore and see how attackers move across identity, cloud, and AI services to exploit security gaps. Through live demonstrations and architectural guidance, the session will show how AWS and CrowdStrike help organizations surface shadow AI; visualize attack paths across code and AI services; stop AI-specific attacks; automate protection workflows; and deliver real-time cloud detection and response (CDR) across modern AI environments. This presentation is brought to you by CrowdStrike, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM224-S": {"abstract": "Vertiv, a global digital infrastructure company, faced fragmented AI experimentation, limited accessibility, and complex enterprise integrational barriers preventing consistent scaling. Vertiv's AI journey began with VeGA, a GenAI platform turned agentic with their recent release of VeGA 3.0. Powered by Amazon Quick, it enables employees to generate content, automate workflows, and create custom applications. In one year, nearly one-third of the workforce was registered in VeGA, spanning functions across all functions and regions. Attendees will learn the architectural blueprint for evolving from basic AI assistants to intelligent agentic systems, including connectors used, data streamlining strategies, and practical implementation steps. This presentation is brought to you by Deloitte, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM225-S": {"abstract": "National Australia Bank (NAB) modernized its digital customer service capability by migrating priority banker groups from legacy messaging platforms to Amazon Connect Chat. The transformation delivered a scalable, integrated, and future-ready messaging environment while improving banker productivity, operational control, and reporting capabilities, and enabling a pathway to enhanced self-service and assisted-service experiences. Deloitte led the end-to-end migration through a structured release approach, encompassing experience design, backlog and epic management, governance, business readiness, training, cutover planning, and operational risk management using AWS services. This session explores the strategy, execution, and lessons learned from delivering a successful enterprise messaging transformation. This presentation is brought to you by Deloitte, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM226-S": {"abstract": "Explore how Generative AI, powered by Proximie and AWS, is fundamentally reshaping the operating room. This session will detail how computer vision and LLMs are creating the OR of the future, supported by Deloitte, to improve productivity and treat more patients in UK NHS Trusts. Attendees will gain insights into the practical application of this powerful alliance and why this innovative approach is vital for the future of healthcare. This presentation is brought to you by Deloitte, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM227-S": {"abstract": "Abstract: PwC-built Generative AI data processing solution for Pacific Life Re, hosted on AWS. The solution automates the ingestion, transformation, validation, schema mapping, and PII redaction of client actuarial datasets that arrive in different formats, languages, and quality levels. In short, it helps PLRe move from manual, time-consuming data preparation to a secure, auditable, AI-enabled workflow that can reduce processing times from weeks to days, improve data quality, and provide clean, validated outputs for actuarial, pricing, and R&D teams. This presentation is brought to you by PwC, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM228-S": {"abstract": "PG&E and PwC will share how they are harnessing AWS to modernize utility operations through AI, automation, and cloud-native engineering. Learn how a unified data and observability foundation delivers real-time operational intelligence, improves system resilience, and enables faster, more informed decision-making. Hear practical lessons on scaling AI responsibly, operationalizing automation, and creating measurable business outcomes across complex enterprise environments. Attendees will leave with a blueprint for transforming traditional operations into intelligent, data-driven services while building a foundation that can support the next wave of generative AI and autonomous operations capabilities. This presentation is brought to you by PwC, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM229-S": {"abstract": "CIOs face a question: where should they invest next to strengthen technology capabilities? Securian Financial Group and PwC built an agentic AI Capability Maturity Measurement Instrument (CMMI) engine using Amazon Quick that turns evidence into a repeatable view of capability gaps, investment priorities, and recommendations across 20 IT domains and 2,000+ capability criteria. The solution ingests documents and surveys, applies consistent scoring, and translates results into prioritized actions spanning skills, resources, processes, and tools. Learn how Securian moved from periodic, manual assessments to an on-demand decision engine that helps technology leaders' direct investment where it matters most. This presentation is brought to you by PwC, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM230-S": {"abstract": "The fastest way to lose control of AI is to let agents multiply without a harness. This talk walks through Presidio's journey from scattered pilots to enterprise-wide adoption, built on a custom orchestration layer that treats cost, identity, and policy as first-class concerns. Attendees will get an inside look at the architectural decisions, guardrails, and economic models that let us scale AI use predictably across the business. If you're weighing governance (cost and risk) against velocity, this is the playbook you want from day one. This presentation is brought to you by Presidio, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM231-S": {"abstract": "Join PwC and four leading clients across industries to hear real examples of how Amazon Connect is transforming customer experience and delivering business outcomes. This session showcases cutting-edge omnichannel solutions across voice, chat, and messaging, along with agentic AI capabilities driving automation in areas like order management and real-time updates. Hear how organizations are deploying next-generation, AI-powered voice solutions in production, with new innovations continuing to emerge. Discover how these advancements deliver measurable business value, backed by PwC's outcome-based approach that ties technology investment directly to efficiency gains and improved customer and business performance. This presentation is brought to you by PwC, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM232-S": {"abstract": "AI that handles on-call autonomously requires agents to take on alert triage, investigations, acting on production, and learning from what happened. Autonomy progresses unevenly as investigations are bottlenecked on quality while actions are limited by trust. In this session we will walk through how we build each primitive of our autonomous agents at Resolve AI, and how we help engineering teams handle on-call and incident resolutions. This presentation is brought to you by Resolve AI, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM233-S": {"abstract": "AI agents can now detect, diagnose, and act in seconds. Observability tells them what is happening. The harder question is how they decide. What is an action worth, and what should an agent optimize for? The intersection of Agentic AIOps and FinOps answers both. The result is a blueprint for business-aware autonomous operations, and three practical steps to apply it in your own environment. This presentation is brought to you by ManageEngine, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM234-S": {"abstract": "We're entering a new era of software operations where the question is no longer whether intelligent agents have a role in production, but whether humans should still be the first responder. As production environments continue to grow more complex, agents are becoming part of the operations team, handling the repetitive work of operating production while engineers focus on the decisions that require judgment, creativity, and experience. This session explores how leading enterprises are rethinking on-call, improving reliability, and reshaping the way production is operated by putting machines on call for humans. This presentation is brought to you by Resolve AI, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM235-S": {"abstract": "Most AI apps put the model and the user on opposite sides of the planet. This talk shows a better pattern: run inference on Amazon Bedrock, and run the agent itself on Cloudflare's edge, within ~50ms of 95% of the world's users. We'll walk through building a working agent with Workers (0ms cold starts), the Agents SDK, and Durable Objects for memory, with AI Gateway in front of Bedrock for caching, rate limiting, cost control, and observability. You'll leave with a reference architecture for shipping fast, cheap, and observable AI to a global audience. This presentation is brought to you by Cloudflare, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM236-S": {"abstract": "Enterprise data is spread across databases, object stores, and compute, but making it usable by AI often requires months of data engineering and a growing web of pipelines to build and maintain. In this session, we’ll show how Eon continuously discovers, connects to, classifies, and transforms data across Amazon RDS, Aurora, DynamoDB, EC2, S3, and more into a unified, AI-ready data layer. We’ll walk through the architecture and semantic layer on AWS, then share how agents can use Amazon Bedrock to query that governed context in natural language through MCP, with Claude, Amazon Quick, and other AI clients. This presentation is brought to you by Eon, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM237-S": {"abstract": "Every SRE knows the pattern: an alert fires, and the next 20 minutes disappear into triage before you've even confirmed what's broken. Context is scattered across dashboards, runbooks, and tribal knowledge, and much of incident response is just reconstructing what already happened. This session explores how autonomous operations changes that story. PagerDuty’s SRE Agent investigates before a human is even involved and proposes fixes you simply approve. See it firsthand through PD Labs, a hands-on site for trying autonomous workflows, and SRE Workbench, launching in early access, where humans, agents, and automation meet in order to investigate, diagnose, and remediate issues. This presentation is brought to you by PagerDuty, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM238-S": {"abstract": "As AI accelerates software development, production systems are changing faster than teams can understand manually. Cognition is closing that gap by giving Devin, its software engineering AI agent running on AWS, access to its own production telemetry through Datadog. Devin uses that context to reason about its production behavior and take action when needed. That feedback loop turns production insights into improvements to Devin’s reliability and future task performance. In this session, we’ll show how Devin investigates alerts, correlates metrics and logs, distinguishes real issues from noise, and uses those insights to improve its harness and workflows. This presentation is brought to you by Datadog, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM239-S": {"abstract": "Hear from a leading U.S. pharmaceutical company on its journey to transforming enterprise AI from isolated experiments into a scalable business capability. Discover how Tech Mahindra helped establish trusted data foundations, harness Agentic AI to enrich product and customer master data, unlock semantic intelligence, and create governed data products that power enterprise-wide insights, including drug demand forecasting. This session will explore the architectural principles, governance strategies, and leadership decisions required to scale compliant, trusted, and value-driven AI. Join Tech Mahindra and a pharma industry leader to learn how data-driven Agentic AI is reshaping the future of the intelligent pharma enterprise. This presentation is brought to you by Tech Mahindra, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM240-S": {"abstract": "The rapid advancement of artificial intelligence directly mirrors the continuous evolution of web intelligence infrastructure. As machine learning models demand exponentially richer datasets, web data extraction has transformed from simple parsing into a sophisticated, mission-critical engineering discipline. In this session, explore how modern web scraping infrastructure actively evolves alongside artificial intelligence to solve live data bottlenecks and complex anti-automation challenges. Discover high-throughput extraction architectures, real-world pipeline designs, and strategic business use cases that turn dynamic web data into production-ready intelligence. Learn how advanced web data infrastructure fuels current artificial intelligence capabilities and shapes the future of automated enterprise decision-making. This presentation is brought to you by Oxylabs, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM241-S": {"abstract": "Agentic AI is moving fast—but isolated agents and one-off experiments won’t transform the enterprise. To create value at scale, companies need a foundation that helps them build and modernize applications faster, orchestration across systems and workflows, governed execution, and control over the infrastructure, performance and cost behind them.​ Join IBM and industry leaders to discover what’s new from IBM on AWS. Hear real-world lessons and measurable business outcomes while exploring the four foundations organizations need to move from disconnected agents to secure, governed, enterprise-wide execution.​ This presentation is brought to you by IBM, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM242-S": {"abstract": "Frontier models can do more than anyone asks of them. At Anthropic, the hardest part of testing a new model is finding work hard enough to make it fail. Outside, most teams hand Claude the tasks they gave last year's model. This session closes that gap: what the newest Claude models do on AWS when you delegate the job, not the task. Multi-day autonomous work, large migrations end to end, agents that verify their results and keep going. Evals, live demos, and how our researchers keep raising the bar. This presentation is brought to you by Anthropic, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM243-S": {"abstract": "Getting a model to work is the easy part. Keeping it fast, cheap, and reliable in production is the hard part. Sai Maddali, Product Manager at Baseten, walks through the platform behind some of the highest-volume inference workloads running today: how GPU capacity is sourced and managed across clouds, how runtimes are tuned per workload, and how dedicated inference, model APIs, and training sit on one pool of compute. He shows why the teams pulling ahead treat build, run, and improve as a single loop, and what that changes about latency, cost, and model quality. This presentation is brought to you by Baseten, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM244-S": {"abstract": "The complexity of problems continues to grow, and smart organizations know that leveraging AI is the quickest way to get this complexity under control and keep customers happy.​ In this session, you’ll see a demo of and learn how to use AI SRE in Splunk Observability Cloud to troubleshoot and remediate problems faster no matter how complex or distributed your operating environment is, all powered by OpenTelemetry. ​ This presentation is brought to you by Splunk, a Cisco Company, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM245-S": {"abstract": "Many AI programs start with a model, a prompt, and a narrow workflow. They stall when agents need to understand permissions, people, policies, past decisions, and data spread across AWS and SaaS systems. This session shows a different path: establish a governed enterprise context layer and scale the enterprise workflows that prove value. Attendees will learn the elements that make up a robust context platform, what to keep open and flexible, and how to measure whether agents improve real work. This presentation is brought to you by Glean, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM246-S": {"abstract": "When a customer calls, a support rep has seconds to understand what they need, what device they're on, and how to solve it fast. Get it right, and you earn trust. Get it wrong, and churn becomes a real risk. T-Mobile closes that gap with agent memory: session context pre-populated before the call starts, enriched turn by turn as it unfolds, with real-time graph traversal connecting customer, device, and issue so the rep sees the full picture. MongoDB Atlas runs it all, from vector search over T-Mobile's knowledge corpus to in-call graph traversal to the live session-memory documents. Afterward, AWS Neptune turns that history into a graph shaping future routing and retention. Walk away with an architecture pattern for building agent memory in real time, and a way to decide what belongs in short-term memory versus what should persist. Featuring T-Mobile, presented by MongoDB. This presentation is brought to you by MongoDB, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM247-S": {"abstract": "Lennar is bringing AI into the everyday work behind more than 80,000 home deliveries a year, from land research and acquisition to construction, customer engagement, and sales. Join Ralph Gootee, CTO of Lennar, and Ariel Assaraf, CEO of Coralogix, for a practical look at moving AI from experimentation into production. They’ll share how Lennar is building and scaling AI agents on Amazon Bedrock, using AWS inference services and open-source models, and how Coralogix helps teams understand adoption, performance, cost, and business impact. This presentation is brought to you by Coralogix, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM248-S": {"abstract": "AI is a catalyst for growth and innovation, yet only 17% of AI initiatives reach full-scale production. Join IBM and AI trailblazers to explore the three-step blueprint for scaling AI on AWS: modernizing the enterprise core across applications, data and infrastructure; fostering a culture that moves innovation forward; and putting digital labor to work in real workflows. Discover how IBM Consulting helps organizations move beyond isolated use cases, accelerate ideas into production and make AI work inside the enterprise, not around it. This presentation is brought to you by IBM, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM249-S": {"abstract": "AI spend often arrives as a black box: a rising bill with little clarity into which teams, models or features drove it. In this breakout, learn how Cloudability helps teams apply FinOps discipline to AI on AWS by categorizing costs, connecting spend to business goals and identifying waste. Discover how we turn that visibility into action for AI workloads running on Amazon EKS, improving GPU efficiency, Kubernetes workload right-sizing and application performance. Then apply the same cost discipline to Amazon Bedrock, including smarter provisioned throughput decisions, so teams can explain, defend and optimize AI spend. This presentation is brought to you by Apptio, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM250-S": {"abstract": "Salesforce Koa is a family of CRM reasoning models post-trained from NVIDIA Nemotron open models. Koa is in production on AWS, inside Salesforce's trust boundary. This session covers technical insights on how Koa was built and how Salesforce serves the model on AWS. Additionally, attendees will learn how Salesforce enforces trust and safety controls in the serving layer outside the model. This session is relevant to any team building and deploying custom open models for the enterprise.", "language": "en"},"AIM251-S": {"abstract": "Connecting an AI agent to enterprise data is easy. Getting it to understand which tables, metrics, definitions and sources to trust is much harder. In this session, learn how Genie Ontology on Databricks combines governed semantics with context automatically learned from queries, dashboards, notebooks and connected systems, then ranks that knowledge by relevance and authority while enforcing user permissions. See how Genie One uses this shared context to reason over live structured and unstructured data, call tools through MCP, take action and deliver more accurate results with less costly agentic exploration on AWS. This presentation is brought to you by Databricks, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM252-S": {"abstract": "AI moves fast until it hits production. Then agents that looked solid in a POC start making calls they shouldn't, hammering the vector database, or failing quietly under load, because the API layer underneath wasn't built for it. This session covers what a strong API foundation does for AI at scale: fine-grained authorization keeps context retrieval inside its data privacy boundaries, touching only what it's permitted to touch; rate limiting protects vector databases from resource exhaustion; edge caching cuts query latency without extra engineering; and circuit breaking plus canary deployments let teams ship changes without compromising security or compliance. You'll leave with architectural blueprints and real enterprise examples showing how the right API foundation turns governance from a blocker into what lets AI teams move faster. Presented by Kong an AWS Partner, alongside FanDuel. This presentation is brought to you by Kong, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM253-S": {"abstract": "Suddenly, everyone is a coder. People who never wrote code now build apps, dashboards, and prototypes with AI, faster than most teams can govern them. The result is shadow AI, ungoverned data, and IP risk. See how a leading global private investment firm gave citizen developers a governed place to build on its existing AWS infrastructure, replacing scattered, unmanaged tools. Learn how approved models, scoped templates, centralized container management, and a complete audit trail let hundreds of builders move fast inside guardrails. Attendees leave with a practical model for governing AI adoption on their own AWS environment. This presentation is brought to you by Coder, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM255-S": {"abstract": "The Access Group is turning petabytes of telemetry from hundreds of teams into an engine for business performance. Its telemetry lake gives teams a clearer view of product health, helping them spot risks sooner, solve problems faster, and understand how technology shapes the customer experience. Join The Access Group CTO Thad Széll and Coralogix CEO Ariel Assaraf to learn how unified telemetry is moving the business from reactive troubleshooting to continuous product improvement. Hear how it is sharpening decisions, focusing teams on what matters most, and creating the trusted data foundation needed to advance The Access Group’s AI ambitions. This presentation is brought to you by Coralogix, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM256-S": {"abstract": "Join Toshish Jawale, Head of AI Engineering at Invoca, to learn how his team is putting context at the center of the business’ customer journeys. Hear how Invoca and Redis are delivering real-time, mutli-source context for Invoca’s agents, how they’re helping customers interact with their brand in exciting ways, and how they’re delivering complete pictures of user brand experiences. This presentation is brought to you by Redis, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM257-S": {"abstract": "What does it actually take to become an AI-native engineering organization? A senior technology executive from a Fortune 500 enterprise sits down with Harness Field CTO Nick Durkin to talk through what it's really taken to go all in on agentic software delivery, orchestrating agents across the entire SDLC instead of one-off automations. They'll get into what that transformation actually looks like end to end, how they decide when an agent runs on its own versus when a human stays in the loop, how agentic engineering has affected cloud migration and consumption, and what it takes to do this at the scale of a Fortune 500 engineering org. This presentation is brought to you by Harness, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM258-S": {"abstract": "TPublishers sit on enormous archives: decades of articles, millions of photos, entire histories of coverage. Most of it is invisible the moment someone needs more than a keyword match. ArcXP built Ask the News to close that gap: a standalone, API-first product giving publishers natural-language access to their own content, powered by MongoDB Atlas Vector Search. The system combines lexical and vector search so results reflect what was meant, not what was said. One of the hardest parts was visual: a pipeline that generated descriptions and embeddings for roughly five million historical images, making decades of archives searchable by meaning for the first time. You'll leave understanding a working pattern for combining lexical and vector search, and a model for exposing natural-language search as an API-first product, not a bolt-on feature. Featuring ArcXP, presented by MongoDB. This presentation is brought to you by MongoDB, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM259-S": {"abstract": "Your agents can't act on yesterday's data. In this session, see how to connect streaming events, governed data, and agent orchestration into one production-ready streamhouse architecture on AWS. Learn how to build a complete, performant, and open streamhouse that delivers real-time context, elastic scale, and mission-critical reliability across every cloud and private environment without data silos. You'll leave with practical patterns for moving from brittle data pipelines to AI built on data streams, designed for speed, trust, and scale. This presentation is brought to you by Confluent, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM260-S": {"abstract": "Enterprises are moving faster with AI than ever. And they're falling further behind. Once the first agents land and the numbers look good, most teams turn to cost control while the frontier keeps moving. This session covers how to do both with Claude on AWS: the security and compliance controls enterprises require, execution inside your own boundary, observability and cost governance, and the safeguards that let you trust agents with more. Then how to keep expanding what agents do as new models arrive, so efficiency doesn't become the ceiling. This presentation is brought to you by Anthropic, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM261-S": {"abstract": "Your traffic outgrows a single cluster long before you expect it to. Colin McGrath explains how Baseten runs inference across more than 80 GPU clusters and roughly 15 cloud providers as one system: how capacity gets found and claimed, how requests get routed to the right region under real load, how large models get delivered to new clusters quickly, and how autoscaling behaves when traffic is bursty and cold starts are expensive. He covers what happens when a whole region goes down, and the patterns that matter most for teams scaling past one cluster. This presentation is brought to you by Baseten, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM262-S": {"abstract": "Every agent call carries cost, permission, and blast radius, and as agents multiply across tools, frameworks, and SaaS, the gaps compound: uncapped spend, unapproved permissions, no shared record. This session breaks down an AI infrastructure layer, running on AWS, that governs every model, agent, and system. A design-time layer publishes an approved catalog of agents, tools, and MCP servers; a runtime layer routes, meters, and enforces policy on every call before it executes. See how spend caps, in-tenant SLMs, and governed APIs turn cost into a controlled input, while one trace gives finance, security, and engineering a shared, audit-ready record. This presentation is brought to you by Boomi, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM263-S": {"abstract": "Most AI agents don't fall apart in production because the model isn't smart enough. They fail because state is fragmented: one agent can't see what another already learned, and nobody can reconstruct what was retrieved, decided, or handed off. In a multi-tenant setting, that's a governance problem, not just a debugging one. This session shows an architecture that fixes it by giving every layer a clear job: Amazon Bedrock AgentCore manages session context and end-to-end tracing, MongoDB Atlas handles durable memory, tenant-aware vector search, and audit history, and the MongoDB MCP Server connects the two so access stays governed. You'll watch agents share state, retrieve tenant-scoped data, and leave a replayable decision trail. Leave with a reference architecture for multi-agent state sharing and a model for what audit-ready really looks like. A MongoDB & AWS technical session. This presentation is brought to you by MongoDB, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM264-S": {"abstract": "In this talk, we’ll walk through an independent eval of Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases, which manages the ingestion, parsing, and retrieval steps in a RAG application. In the first half, we’ll cover our methodology, including how we developed a dataset that queries documents such as tickets, wiki pages, and product docs, and what we decided to score: latency, cost, relevance, and citation support. We’ll also cover how we analyzed the results with research rigor, including p50 and p95 latency and confidence intervals around our metrics. In the second half, we’ll expand this into a conceptual understanding of evals and observability: why they’re important, how other companies are implementing them in production, and the terminology you need to know. This presentation is brought to you by Braintrust, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM265-S": {"abstract": "Observability's real job has always been closing the feedback loop between what you ship and what happens next. We'll trace how that loop evolved at Honeycomb: from dashboards you stared at, to SLOs that quantified what mattered, to Canvas, agents that investigate with you, and now MCP tools feeding production reality straight back into software written by agents This presentation is brought to you by Honeycomb, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM266-S": {"abstract": "Every leader is under pressure to show AI value now. Some move fast, and agents sprawl across teams with no shared controls. Others lock everything down, and pilots never reach production. Both point to the same gap: governance maturity hasn't kept pace with agent speed. This talk covers how governance becomes an accelerator, not a blocker, to production AI. You’ll learn how to design identity, policy, and guardrails from day one, so agents ship with the same controls whether they run on AWS Bedrock, hybrid, or otherwise. Get the principles right early, and agents move from pilot to production without every team reinventing governance on their own. Takeaways: Why AI programs sprawl or stall, and what governance maturity looks like in between. How trusted AI governance turns into speed instead of slowing teams down. What governance principles to design in from day one, on AWS & beyond. This presentation is brought to you by WSO2, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM267-S": {"abstract": "Your AI pilot ran smoothly and stayed on budget. Then you launched, and the invoice was much higher than the estimate. This session breaks down why that happens and what to do about it. We'll walk through where AI spend actually goes once a system leaves the demo stage, why agentic AI costs differently than a simple chatbot, and how choosing the right model for each task, not just the flagship model for everything, can cut spend dramatically without hurting quality. You'll leave with a practical framework for tracking cost, avoiding common budgeting traps, and having a more confident conversation with finance the next time AI spend comes up. This presentation is brought to you by Mission Cloud, a CDW Company, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM268-S": {"abstract": "Every organization is building their AI architecture in real-time: deciding which agents to use, which data sources to connect them to, and figuring how to get teams to collaborate across it all. These different layers have been arranged over many years of procuring tools, but can sometimes feel like a jumbled mess in the AI era. This session offers a practical way to reexamine your tech architecture. We'll cover four patterns that recur across organizations as they try to structure their business for the AI era, plus pitfalls to avoid to ensure your tech stack is optimized for AI. This presentation is brought to you by Notion, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM269-S": {"abstract": "AI agents are moving from pilots into production faster than most organizations can govern them, and independent teams building in parallel are creating what practitioners now call agent sprawl. This session presents a repeatable 90-day pattern that converts sprawl into governed agents ready for production, using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, Guardrails, and Kiro alongside NIST AI RMF and the Well-Architected Generative AI Lens. Architects, platform owners, and public-sector leaders see how a governed runtime, evidence-based mission KPIs, and cost discipline turn compliance into an accelerator. Audit-ready patterns from CDW customer engagements across regulated commercial and public-sector missions are included This presentation is brought to you by Mission Cloud, a CDW Company, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM270-S": {"abstract": "Deepfakes are transforming the rules of trust. As AI-generated voice, video, and imagery become easier to create, attackers use synthetic media to make deception feel familiar, urgent, and credible. In this session, KnowBe4 shows how deepfakes fit into broader social engineering campaigns built around narrative, timing, and cross-channel reinforcement. The fake clip is rarely the whole attack; it is one piece of a larger story designed to short-circuit judgment when it matters most. Attendees will learn what separates an interesting tech demo from a nation-state-level attack. They will see how these attacks work and why convincing stories and cognitive biases override technical skepticism even in well-trained people. Perry Carpenter will also cover how organizations can prepare for high-stakes moments when trust is under pressure—before the call comes in, not after This presentation is brought to you by KnowBe4, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM271-S": {"abstract": "United and ZS go behind the scenes of the data, AI and technology powering personalized flight stories for travelers at scale. This presentation is brought to you by ZS, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM272-S": {"abstract": "Most organizations can tell you what they spend on AI. Fewer can tell you what they're getting for it. FinOps for AI closes that gap, but it takes three things: visibility into spend by use case; controls that act on what the data tells you instead of just surfacing it; and value tracking that connects spend to outcomes your stakeholders can evaluate. This session includes real examples of token attribution, guardrail patterns that respond to data, and a model for turning ROI signals into corrective action. This presentation is brought to you by Kion, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM273-S": {"abstract": "Agentic coding loops let AI develop, test, and iterate on code autonomously. But agents often lack the permissions required to validate how code behaves in the cloud, stalling the cycle and holding back velocity. This session will show how simulating your AWS application environments locally can enable AI agents to identify and fix bugs faster, more securely, and more effectively than human engineers can when building in live cloud development environments. This presentation is brought to you by LocalStack, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM274-S": {"abstract": "AI for SRE isn’t just a speed or accuracy problem; it’s a problem of deeper understanding. This session explores how team members across different domains in an enterprise can use a shared AI reasoning layer to operate production systems and collaborate effectively to increase reliability. We’ll show how this AI reasoning layer handles the extremes of alert storms and alert silence, catching deployment-triggered anomalies before they cause production impact. Learn how teams are moving beyond reactive dashboards, using state-of-the-art techniques to instantly correlate cross-domain telemetry, execute complex investigations, and achieve proactive reliability in dynamic cloud and hybrid environments. This presentation is brought to you by Ciroos, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM275-S": {"abstract": "AWS Marketplace isn't just a procurement channel, it's a financial lever. A typical ISV saves a procurement cycle. Cisco draws down committed spend against the infrastructure your agents run on: connectivity from cloud to edge, visibility into agent behavior, and protection for models, identities, and data. Partners add the expertise to deploy it right, turning a procurement decision into an architectural one, a true better together win with AWS. This presentation is brought to you by Cisco, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"},"AIM277-S": {"abstract": "This session explores how Vercel Enterprise customers can run workloads in their own AWS account while continuing to use the Vercel developer experience. You’ll learn about the separation between the Vercel control plane and customer runtime, and why this model can help organizations meet data privacy, security, and compliance requirements. You’ll see how the setup works through a live walkthrough and demo, and how this architecture can support broader access to tools like v0, Amazon Q, and other coding agents. This presentation is brought to you by Vercel, an AWS Partner.", "language": "en"}};
  window.APP_DATA.sessions.forEach(function (s) {
    var x = m[s.session_id];
    if (x) for (var k in x) if (x[k]) s[k] = x[k];
  });
})();
